==Exception Handling (Multiple Catch Blocks or Multi-Catch)
Java allows handling multiple exceptions using either separate catch blocks or a multi-catch
block.
try {
// transaction code
} catch (InsufficientFundsException e) {
System.out.println("Not enough balance.");
} catch (InvalidAccountException e) {
System.out.println("Account not found.");
} catch (NetworkFailureException e) {
System.out.println("Network error. Please try again.");
} catch (Exception e) {
System.out.println("An unexpected error occurred.");
}
Alternative using multi-catch:
try {
// transaction code
} catch (InsufficientFundsException | InvalidAccountException | NetworkFailureException e)
{
System.out.println("Transaction failed: " + e.getMessage());
}
