16) A payment gateway processes multiple types of transactions. While
executing a transaction, different exceptions may occur, such as Insufficient
Balance Exception, Invalid Card Exception, or Transaction Time out Exception.
The system must handle all these exceptions to ensure smooth transactions.
Question: How can multiple exceptions be handled in Java to make sure the
payment gateway runs without failure? Provide a suitable example.
=== In Java, multiple exceptions can be handled using multiple catch blocks or a multi-catch
feature (since Java 7), which allows you to catch several exceptions in a single catch block. To
ensure smooth transactions in a payment gateway, the system must handle specific
exceptions like InsufficientBalanceException, InvalidCardException, and
TransactionTimeoutException.
Example:
class PaymentGateway {
public void processTransaction(double balance, String cardDetails) throws Exception {
try {
if (balance <= 0) {
throw new InsufficientBalanceException("Insufficient balance in the account.");
}
if (cardDetails == null || cardDetails.isEmpty()) {
throw new InvalidCardException("Card details are invalid.");
}
if (Math.random() > 0.95) { // Simulate a transaction timeout
throw new TransactionTimeoutException("Transaction timed out.");
}
System.out.println("Transaction successful!");
} catch (InsufficientBalanceException | InvalidCardException |
TransactionTimeoutException e) {
System.out.println("Error: " + e.getMessage());
} catch (Exception e) {
System.out.println("Unexpected error: " + e.getMessage());
}
}
// Custom exceptions
class InsufficientBalanceException extends Exception {
public InsufficientBalanceException(String message) {
super(message);
}
}
class InvalidCardException extends Exception {
public InvalidCardException(String message) {
super(message);
}
}
class TransactionTimeoutException extends Exception {
public TransactionTimeoutException(String message) {
super(message);
}
}
public static void main(String[] args) {
PaymentGateway gateway = new PaymentGateway();
try {
gateway.processTransaction(500, "Card123");
} catch (Exception e) {
System.out.println("Main error handler: " + e.getMessage());
}
}
}
